plugin-hostd (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New tool plugin-hostd-probe: it starts a program that loads a plugin
    (clap-qualify by default) under limits of CPU time, memory, open files,
    file size and real-time priority, kills the whole process tree on the
    deadline, and writes the facts of the run as a JSON document. Its
    manual page is installed, and plugin-hostd-dev ships the document's
    schema in /usr/share/plugin-hostd/probe-output.schema.json.
  * Notes: the instance verbs note_input, note_on, note_off and
    all_notes_off pass notes to a worker that takes them; an effect answers
    -513, and an LV2 instance on mod-host answers -514 (play it through its
    JACK MIDI port).
  * The tempo and transport (set_bpm, set_bpb, transport, transport_sync)
    are kept by the daemon and handed to every worker when it starts or
    restarts.
  * Presets: preset_list and preset_get list an instance's presets by the
    key preset_load takes; an LV2 instance on mod-host answers -515.
  * The events param_gesture and remote_page_suggest are relayed. When a
    worker dies or an instance is removed in the middle of a gesture, the
    daemon sends the gesture's end itself.
  * Under lv2_worker auto, a plugin the adapter refused is asked again after
    lv2_worker_set, pin_set, pin_accept or pin_clear.
  * param_info on a CLAP instance passes the worker's answer through; -511
    (no checked unit and scale) is documented.
  * libmod-host-protocol0 0.1.0-6~fmx or newer is required: older builds
    hang on a command of exactly the socket's buffer size and run only the
    first of several commands that arrive in one read.
  * A worker line too long to relay is now dropped whole; before, its tail
    reached the controller as a line of its own.
  * Numbers are refused when written as -0, so zero has a single spelling.
  * The package builds without omx-clap-core; omx-clap-host-tests is
    needed only to run the tests.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

plugin-hostd (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * You choose which program runs LV2 plugins: mod-host, omx-clap-host or
    auto (the setting lv2_worker, changed with the lv2_worker_set command).
    A host that cannot take LV2 plugins now answers with a new error (-512)
    and the daemon announces the refusal with the lv2_adapter_refused event.
  * omx-clap-host 0.9.0 or newer is recommended: older versions do not load
    LV2 plugins, so with the default auto choice everything would run on
    mod-host.
  * A new page explains how to use plugin-hostd in your own host.
  * Fixed a build failure of programs that include pin.h with gcc -O3
    -Werror.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

